# chat at 12x60 (the flat tier, TUI-DESIGN-2 §4.1): JEVCODE_MOCK_INTAKE=ambiguous — `the date parsing` draws the intake's
# one-row twin in its 39-cell ladder form `run this as a task?  [y] [n]  Esc keeps` (§3.7 `intakeRowLines` below 72
# columns), never a card; Enter before the arm is inert, `n` after the arm takes the chat reading and a [jevcode] reply
# follows; no run. The narrow status row may drop the `sess` badge, so the `[sandbox]` item stands in for the attached host.
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect Say hi
expect \[sandbox\]
sleep 0.3
send the date parsing
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect run this as a task\?  \[y\] \[n\]  Esc keeps
send \r
sleep 0.25
send n
expect \[jevcode\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* 
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
